Author: Alex Nelson <a.nelson@prometheuscomputing.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 24 10:37:28 2013 -0400

    fiwalk: Update rusage reporting
    
    The <runstats> element was an early version of a resource usage report.
    Later versions, particularly the one employed by Hashdeep, simply use an
    <rusage> element with no renaming of its fields, and an extra
    <clocktime> element.
    
    This change makes Fiwalk output a consistent element with Hashdeep and
    the DFXML C++ library.  It adds precision and programmatic access to the
    elapsed time record.
    
    This and the prior patch also cause Fiwalk's output to validate against
    the DFXML schema version here:
    <https://github.com/ajnelson/dfxml_schema/tree/archive/for_hashdeep_v1>
    
    Adding getrusage shouldn't cause any problems elsewhere in the codebase;
    the HAVE_GETRUSAGE symbol doesn't appear anywhere.
    
    (This change does not use the DFXML library code included in the same
    directory, because that is a less-than-straightforward inclusion. A
    future patch should make use of dfxml.{h,cpp} as libraries.)
    
    Signed-off-by: Alex Nelson <a.nelson@prometheuscomputing.com>

